<!--
    kuna calleeretpurge, ObjC: `objc_msgSend_stret` pops the hidden result
    pointer.

    On i386 the ObjC message senders that return a structure in memory take
    the result pointer as a hidden first argument and pop it with `ret $4`,
    like any struct-returning function, and the caller is compiled around that.
    They are imports, so there is no body to read the `ret $4` from: IDA
    special-cases the three names (pc.so 0x37670). The caller here is the
    i386 gcc -O2 `use` of kuna-calleeretpurge-x86.xml, with its callee
    replaced by an import stub (`jmp [slot]`) named `_objc_msgSend_stret`.

    Stage: P4 call prototypes (ActionExtraPopSetup), option calleeretpurge
    off|on. Pass 1 (off) pins the bug, pass 2 (on, the default) the fix.
-->
